(3602769, 504327, 46336, '<td valign="top">Or just one poppie, occassionally rotated aand flipped. I do like your presentation of the three images, and the two internal borders. The yellow poppie works best for em. I wonder what the whole would look like if all the images were yellow.</td>', 'Or just one poppie, occassionally rotated aand flipped. I do like your presentation of the three images, and the two internal borders. The yellow poppie works best for em. I wonder what the whole would look like if all the images were yellow.', '2007-05-01 22:16:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3602811, 505105, 47852, '<td valign="top">Nice set of shots to show the action, but the editing is too obvious for my tastes.  You can the halo around her body and the racquet where you''ve edited, perhaps where you tried to add a blur to the background or tried to make the ground/wall even up a bit?  Just needs a bit more editing to clean it up and make it even better!  Still, a fun shot! :)</td>', 'Nice set of shots to show the action, but the editing is too obvious for my tastes.  You can the halo around her body and the racquet where you''ve edited, perhaps where you tried to add a blur to the background or tried to make the ground/wall even up a bit?  Just needs a bit more editing to clean it up and make it even better!  Still, a fun shot! :)', '2007-05-01 22:25:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3602905, 504114, 65035, '<td valign="top">I waited until I''d voted the whole challenge before coming back to comment on this one, it''s my absolute favorite of the challenge and I wanted to sit with it awhile. It was love at first sight but like any love the slight discords keep it interesting. The middle image being slightly off centre bothered me a little until I realized that if it was centre the reds would overlap and that wouldn''t work as well, so it shows care in the composition and respect for the way the images work as a whole. That slight discord is one of the charms of this image, it draws my eye to inspect the corners of each image as well as the whole. I love the way the blown whites on the top image meld it with the background. The blue draws my eye in an opposing triangle to the red and the rust in the top image leads my eye into the rust stain in the bottom one to join the images and yet each image retains a strength and individuality of it''s own. This should be hanging in a gallery, huge, with a comfy chair so that people can sit and get lost in the details of it at their leisure. I have no doubt that it will be under appreciated so let me congratulate you now on a fine piece of work.</td>', 'I waited until I''d voted the whole challenge before coming back to comment on this one, it''s my absolute favorite of the challenge and I wanted to sit with it awhile. It was love at first sight but like any love the slight discords keep it interesting. The middle image being slightly off centre bothered me a little until I realized that if it was centre the reds would overlap and that wouldn''t work as well, so it shows care in the composition and respect for the way the images work as a whole. That slight discord is one of the charms of this image, it draws my eye to inspect the corners of each image as well as the whole. I love the way the blown whites on the top image meld it with the background. The blue draws my eye in an opposing triangle to the red and the rust in the top image leads my eye into the rust stain in the bottom one to join the images and yet each image retains a strength and individuality of it''s own. This should be hanging in a gallery, huge, with a comfy chair so that people can sit and get lost in the details of it at their leisure. I have no doubt that it will be under appreciated so let me congratulate you now on a fine piece of work.', '2007-05-01 22:42:03.000000', NULL, 1),
