(3622529, 504173, 30982, '<td valign="top">I''d say it did OK.  It must be the Toole family charm.  :-)  Oh, and I still hope you don''t actually go anywhere in those shoes...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-05-07 00:07:28.</i></td>', 'I''d say it did OK.  It must be the Toole family charm.  :-)  Oh, and I still hope you don''t actually go anywhere in those shoes...', '2007-05-07 01:06:53.000000', '2007-05-07 01:07:28.000000', 0),
(3622532, 504548, 36006, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TooCool:</b></div><hr/><i> Nicely done!  Bottom right shot looks a bit underexposed though.<br/>TC </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No, I disagree. If you look at the grass on all three panels, the levels are fine.<br/> <br/>If the panel in question was underexposed, the surrounding grass would not be exposed equally as the other two panels.<br/> <br/>These images were shot the same day, the same time, the same field, the same two teams, and edited in RAW the same way.<br/> <br/>I guess you missed this little detail.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by TooCool: Nicely done!  Bottom right shot looks a bit underexposed though.TC   No, I disagree. If you look at the grass on all three panels, the levels are fine. If the panel in question was underexposed, the surrounding grass would not be exposed equally as the other two panels. These images were shot the same day, the same time, the same field, the same two teams, and edited in RAW the same way. I guess you missed this little detail. ', '2007-05-07 01:07:43.000000', NULL, 0),
